# Copy to .env.local and fill in. .env.local is gitignored.
#
# LOCAL DEVELOPMENT NEEDS ONLY DATABASE_URL.
# Everything below it is optional until you deploy.

# --- required locally -------------------------------------------------------

# Matches docker-compose.yml. Port 5433 to avoid colliding with any other Postgres.
DATABASE_URL=postgres://survivor:localdev@localhost:5433/survivor

# The deployed database, kept SEPARATE from DATABASE_URL on purpose. Local
# commands keep using the Docker database, so `npm run demo` or `db:nuke` can
# never reach real player data. Deployment sets this value as its DATABASE_URL.
# PRODUCTION_DATABASE_URL=postgresql://...neon.tech/neondb?sslmode=require

# NOTE: there is deliberately no AUTH_SECRET. Sessions do not use signed
# cookies -- the cookie carries a 32-byte random token and only its SHA-256
# hash is stored server-side, so there is nothing to sign. See src/lib/auth.ts.

# --- optional locally -------------------------------------------------------

# Email.
#
# UNSET  -> mail is written to ./tmp/mail as readable HTML and the path printed
#           to the console. No provider or domain needed; good for development.
# SET    -> mail is really delivered via Resend. MAIL_FROM must be an address on
#           a domain verified in Resend; no mailbox needs to exist there.
#
# MAIL_FROM needs quotes because it contains spaces. The others do not.
# RESEND_API_KEY=
# MAIL_FROM="Survivor League <commissioner@example.com>"
#
# Where player replies go. The sending domain has receiving switched off, so
# without this a reply disappears silently. Point it at an inbox you read.
# REPLY_TO=you@gmail.com

# Shared secret required by the scheduled-job endpoints, so only the cron
# trigger can invoke them. Generate a long random value before deploying.
# JOB_TRIGGER_SECRET=

# NFL schedule, scores AND point spreads all come from ESPN's public endpoints
# and need no key at all (D29). There is no odds vendor in this stack.
#
# ESPN refuses requests from Vercel AND from Cloudflare Workers (D34, D35), so
# the deployed app cannot reach it at all. Schedule and week structure are
# therefore synced from a machine ESPN will talk to, using `npm run sync:prod`.
# There is deliberately no proxy setting: one was built, tested, blocked, and
# removed, because a stale proxy value silently broke a working local sync.

# Scores and point spreads come from The Odds API, which is keyed and works from
# any server. This is what the scheduled jobs use. Free tier: 500 credits/month;
# a full season needs well under 100.
# ODDS_API_KEY=
